1. Scope

This license applies to the OmniNorm software, including its source code, documentation, and associated materials distributed as part of this repository (collectively, the “Software”).

OmniNorm was originally developed by Francesco Gualdrini.

The name “OmniNorm” refers to the normalization methodology and its reference implementation distributed through the official OmniNorm repository.

2. Non-Commercial Research Use

Permission is granted, free of charge, to use, copy, and modify the Software for:

* academic research;
* scientific research conducted by non-profit or public research organizations;
* educational purposes;
* personal, non-commercial research and evaluation.

Such use is permitted regardless of whether the resulting research is subsequently published, subject to the citation requirements described below.

Use of the Software by an academic, educational, non-profit, or public research organization remains permitted when the research receives external or industry funding, provided that the Software itself is not being used to provide a commercial product or service on behalf of, or primarily for the commercial benefit of, a third party.

3. Scientific Publications and Citation

Scientific results generated, processed, normalized, analyzed, or otherwise materially supported using OmniNorm may be published.

Any scientific publication in which OmniNorm materially contributes to the generation or analysis of reported results must appropriately acknowledge and cite OmniNorm.

Users must cite the designated OmniNorm scientific publication when one is specified by the copyright holder.

If no designated scientific publication is available, users must cite the OmniNorm software repository and, where available, the specific software version and/or archived DOI used in the analysis.

Citation or acknowledgement of OmniNorm does not imply endorsement of the resulting research by the copyright holder.

4. Commercial Use

Commercial use of the Software is not permitted under this license.

For the purposes of this license, commercial use includes, but is not limited to:

* use of the Software as part of a commercial product or service;
* use of the Software to provide paid data-analysis, consulting, diagnostic, pharmaceutical, biotechnology, or other commercial services;
* incorporation of the Software or substantial portions of it into software distributed commercially;
* use of the Software primarily for commercial advantage or monetary compensation;
* internal use by a for-profit organization when the use directly supports commercial research, product development, commercial decision-making, or provision of commercial services.

Commercial use requires a separate written license or explicit written permission from the copyright holder.

For commercial licensing inquiries, contact the copyright holder.

5. Modification

Users may modify the Software for purposes permitted by this license.

Modified versions must be clearly identified as modified and must not be represented as the original OmniNorm software, reference implementation, or methodology.

Any scientific publication using a modified version must clearly state that the Software was modified when those modifications could materially affect the analysis or interpretation of the results.

Modification of the Software does not remove the citation requirements of this license when the modified software is derived substantially from OmniNorm.

